{"content":"# Thread 1 — 🚨 BLOCKING: unguarded `dispatchCiWorkflow` in the zombie re-dispatch path

**Fixed** — commit `06dc4833` (`js/smAgent.js`, zombie re-dispatch path).

The dispatch is now wrapped in its own try/catch, exactly per the suggested shape:

```js
dropOpenPrsCache(effectiveRepoInfo);
try {
    dispatchCiWorkflow(ticket.branch);
} catch (eZci) {
    console.warn('  ⚠️  zombie re-dispatch failed for ' + key + ': ' +
                 (eZci.message || eZci) + ' — re-arming, retry next tick');
    try {
        if (!DRY) {
            github_add_labels({ ... labels: ['ai_validating'] });
        }
    } catch (eZre2) { /* validate-armed re-arms next tick anyway */ }
    continue;
}
```

- The whole SM tick survives a throwing dispatch — the exception no longer reaches the tickets loop or `processRule`'s `rules.forEach`.
- On failure the PR **re-acquires `ai_validating`**, so it keeps its serialization slot and the next tick retries as a zombie (no re-entry through the `validate-armed` arm race).
- `continue` fires **before** the marker comment / `stampValidationChecksForModule`, so a lost dispatch never counts toward the crash-loop cap (the counter under-count you flagged is gone by construction).

TDD: new test `gh-821: a THROWING zombie re-dispatch must NOT kill the SM tick — arm re-acquired, next PR still processed` was verified RED on the pre-fix engine (the error escaped `sm.action`) and GREEN after the fix. Pattern check: the only other `dispatchCiWorkflow` call site (`validate_pr`) already wraps the identical call in its whole-body try/catch.
